== the daemon pins release 'v3.2.0-dev.2537+45412c2' at 'http://127.0.0.1:4302/releases'
== GET /cli/install.sh: public (no credential), headers, HEAD
### GET without a credential
$ sh -c curl -s -D - -o /dev/null http://127.0.0.1:4301/cli/install.sh | tr -d '\r' | grep -iE '^(HTTP|content-type|cache-control|x-content-type-options)'
    HTTP/1.1 200 OK
    Cache-Control: no-store
    Content-Type: text/x-shellscript; charset=utf-8
    X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
    -> exit=0
### GET with a wrong bearer
$ curl -s -o /dev/null -w %{http_code}\n -H Authorization: Bearer nope http://127.0.0.1:4301/cli/install.sh
    200
    -> exit=0
### GET with the access code
$ curl -s -o /dev/null -w %{http_code}\n -H Authorization: Bearer <access-code> http://127.0.0.1:4301/cli/install.sh
    200
    -> exit=0
### HEAD
$ curl -s -I -o /dev/null -w %{http_code}\n http://127.0.0.1:4301/cli/install.sh
    200
    -> exit=0
### served script holds no access code
$ sh -c curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:4301/cli/install.sh | grep -c -- '<access-code>' || true
    0
    -> exit=0
### shellcheck-free syntax check (sh -n)
$ sh -c curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:4301/cli/install.sh | sh -n && echo ok
    ok
    -> exit=0
